WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.790
Hey everybody, happy new year! So 2016 has come to a close so it's time to talk about all

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.440
the dead characters on Game of Thrones that we want back.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.520
So this is going to be my top 10 list and I know you're all wondering about when the

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.630
next trailer is going to come.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.740
So I tried to include some of that at the end of this too.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.250
Just careful for spoilers for everything that's happened on the show so far, and there is a new

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.990
round of the Game of Thrones giveaway. They
just released enhanced editions of the book,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.300
so, it's basically for the value of those
enhanced editions.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.060
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video. Be sure

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.820
to click that bell to enable alerts so you
don't miss anything.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.170
So a lot of times characters are killed off
in big twist moments to shock the audience

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.770
to remind you that no one is safe.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.579
Anybody can be killed.

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:45.140
Sometimes they're killed off because the writers
write themselves into a corner and they can't

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.680
think of anywhere else to take the character,
and sometimes they're killed off because they're

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.289
overpowered or they have too much knowledge
and they become a crutch for other characters

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:58.550
to lean on - that the writers don't want the other
characters to have.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.850
So Barristan Selmy for instance was a crutch
for Daenerys to lean on.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.220
He had so much experience,

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.820
so much knowledge. He knew all about Rhaegar
Targaryen somebody who we need a lot more

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.220
information about, so naturally the writers
took him away.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.560
So let's go through this list, and all explained for
the characters on the show that are dead,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.130
but are still alive in the books, why it is
I think that they killed them on the show.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:27.490
The quote from George RR Martin says it
all - 2016 was directed by me. I'm sorry. So,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.880
so many people we've lost,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.310
so let's remember some of the really cool
ones.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:37.510
Number 10 - Doran Martell, an amazing book character
but was probably killed off on the show because

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.610
the writers wrote themselves into a corner
with the Dorne storyline.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.310
It's a really big storyline in the books,
but on the TV show they don't have that much

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:47.940
time to focus on it.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.369
So it seems like they were just stepping around
it because they wanted to use a couple of

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:57.259
the Sand Snake characters but they had all
this stuff that was happening down south and

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:02.119
they needed to find a way to not have to go
back there on a regular basis to explain what

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.180
was going on.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.880
So naturally, if the Sand Snakes were on the
loose, he would've sent an army after them

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.349
to stop them from causing more chaos.

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:12.560
So what do you do, you have to kill him.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.040
So it totally sucks.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:19.100
This also had the unintended consequence of
making the Dorne storyline even more hated

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.459
than it already was.

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:22.959
So even though "Game of Thrones" is an amazing
show,

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:27.790
not all the storylines shine like Lannister
gold. Every once in a while they run into problems

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:33.879
just like any other TV show. So may you rest
in peace Dornish master plan. In the books,

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:38.900
the idea of the Dornish master plan is that
Doran was secretly working as part of this

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.680
conspiracy to put a Targaryen back on the
throne and was arranging to have one of his

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.090
children, Quentyn, marry Daenerys to form an alliance.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.690
But like the TV show changing things from
the books, Quentyn was excised from the story,

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:58.790
Trystane was murdered by the Sand Snakes trying
to end the Martell regime. It seems like there

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.800
aren't any Martells left, so who has power
now, the Sand Snakes? Is there open revolt in

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.800
the streets?

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.700
We have no idea. Number nine - Shireen Baratheon,
this is one of the saddest deaths on the

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:16.760
show. But it proved great fuel for Ser Davos 
to go after Melisandre. So, she's still alive

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.319
in the books, but it sounds like she might
meet the same fate.

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:23.951
The reason that Dan and Dave said that they
killed her off on the show in the way that

00:03:23.951 --> 00:03:29.299
they did, like having Stannis execute her as
an offering to the Red God to ensure their

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:33.830
victory, which didn't really come, at least
not the way they expected it against the forces of

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:39.620
the Boltons, is because they felt like Stannis
had crossed the line and was committed to

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:40.620
his cause.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.870
He was so stubborn that he was not going to
waiver.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.860
So when Melisandre put it to him,

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.310
we need royal blood,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:52.510
he offered up Shireen. The reason I think they
couldn't use his wife Selyse is because

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:57.049
her blood did not flow from Stannis as that
was the whole idea of the king's blood flowed

00:03:57.049 --> 00:04:00.350
through Shireen's veins because it came from
Stannis.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:05.080
So, it was mostly a death that was born out of
the logic of Stannis's course on the TV show

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:10.720
and provided like a really big shocking moment
in sort of the first ice block in the giant

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:16.190
wall that was Melisandre misinterpreting
visions and her perceived downfall.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.430
She's down but not out.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.799
We'll have to talk about Melisandre stuff in
another video because she was still effective

00:04:21.799 --> 00:04:23.800
in bringing Jon Snow back from the dead.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.190
So she does have power, but she misinterprets
her visions.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:33.480
So sadly led to Shireen being sacrificed. Number
eight - Barristan Selmy, another really terrible

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.590
death, he's an amazing character that's still
alive in the books. He's supposed to have his

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:43.800
own POV chapter during "Winds of Winter". The problem
 is that he was this huge crutch for Daenerys,

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.800
like I said.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.840
So the writers wanted a big shocking moment
they wanted her to feel alone, so they took

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:49.940
that away.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.900
So, that was sort of paving the way for her new
small counsel with Tyrion to come in.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.990
So we're starting to see this thing where, you know, Daenerys has three dragons, she has this very

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:04.340
good advisor Tyrion, but slowly and slowly
she's gotten more and more powerful.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.300
So the writers have started to take stuff away
from her. That might continue into season seven

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.120
If she seems invincible,

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:16.240
there's no way that's gonna last. So, whatever
her crutches, her dragons, her advisors, those

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.810
will slowly go away over the course of the
next two seasons.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:25.400
It would really suck if my 2017 "Characters
That We Want Back" list included a dragon on

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:30.020
it. But number seven - The Blackfish went out
like a champ. I know a lot of people are like,

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.520
hey we didn't see a body, he's not dead.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.360
The idea was, is that he was going to fight
off the Lannister army 'til he was killed.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.210
Jaime didn't really have much use for The
Blackfish because Edmure controlled the castle

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.990
and he had capitulated.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.210
So the Lannisters were already in control.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:51.180
So this is another one of those Stannis-type
death moments, where they imply that he's going

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.180
to be killed.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.020
But they don't just out right show it to you.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.320
So you're just left to wonder.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.270
I think The Blackfish is dead - I think that was
the whole idea of that last scene with Brienne.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.790
So may you rest in peace Blackfish - you sass
like a champ!

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:09.880
He was one of the funniest, most Monty Python
things about the season. So, number six -

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.850
Mance Rayder - we have not seen him in a while, but
he is so much cooler in the books. He becomes

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:19.510
a much bigger part of them trying to retake
Winterfell from the Boltons.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:22.039
He infiltrates it using "glamour".

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:27.360
So the only thing the show has done with glamour
thus far is just show us Melisandre's jewel.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.240
Just show us like the 200-year-old lady that
she really is,

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.510
even though she's been using that jewel
to stay young.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:37.210
That's part of the glamour process - like you
have to have that next to your skin in order

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:42.340
for it to work. But the show probably killed
Mance off because it wasn't going to be doing

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.660
a lot of his storyline.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:47.400
There were just a lot of characters involved in
that northern plot that they weren't going to

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.479
do on the show.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:50.220
So there wasn't much reason to keep him around.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.810
They didn't want him to be as grand of a
figure - they wanted the conflict between the brotherhood

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.180
and the Wildlings to devolve into Jon Snow's
death.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.949
So if Mance were still around,

00:06:59.949 --> 00:07:03.630
then that probably wouldn't have happened, like
he probably would've helped keep things under

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:09.851
control. So, number five - Maester Aemon, a Targaryen
alone in the world is a terrible thing. So

00:07:09.851 --> 00:07:11.960
he was another one of those characters

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:17.030
that was a crutch for Jon Snow to lean on.
He's on his path to becoming a leader in his

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.030
own right.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:24.030
So naturally, like Daenerys lost Barristan Selmy, Jon Snow lost Maester Aemon, may he rest

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:29.660
in peace. The actor playing him also passed
away after they had filmed most of his scenes.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.061
So it was very sad, but he lived a very long
life.

00:07:32.061 --> 00:07:37.919
Maester Aemon, even in the context of the show,
had lived an extremely long life. He has this

00:07:37.919 --> 00:07:43.090
really interesting backstory that I'll do
another video sometime soon, but his brother

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:50.270
was Egg from the "Dunk and Egg" series who ascended
the Iron Throne because Maester Aemon was in line

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:55.699
ahead of him, but chose to abdicate because he
didn't want to create another Targaryen civil

00:07:55.699 --> 00:07:58.340
war, where all of his brothers would end up
dying.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:02.879
So he took the black, went to the wall, became
a maester. That is kind of fun to think about,

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:08.330
what would that have looked like, Maester Aemon sitting
on the Iron Throne. Number four - Stannis Baratheon.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:13.039
A lot of people were really upset when the show
killed him off. He's still alive in the books.

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:18.480
They're getting ready for sort of their episode
nine, "Battle of the Bastards"-type episode.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.419
But in the books I'm referring to it as the
Battle of Winterfell, Stannis is getting ready

00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:27.600
for that, but ultimately I think, you know, because
he's not destined to sit on the Iron Throne,

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.650
he will be killed off of eventually.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:34.430
So the show was just making a beeline for
that. Stannis, as Melisandre believed it, was

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.469
not the "Prince who was Promised". That is someone
else, she starts to believe in Jon Snow, that

00:08:39.469 --> 00:08:42.519
he comes back, and now it seems like that's
him.

00:08:42.519 --> 00:08:46.960
He's the one that's destined to rise up. So,
the question now remains, how is Stannis going

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:50.670
to die in the books? Is it gonna happen in a similar
way? Will he fall?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.100
He was one of the best characters on the show,
even though he was an asshole 'til the day

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.100
he died.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.980
He was just so much fun.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:03.610
But, number three is Catelyn Stark, for obvious
reasons, for Lady Stoneheart reasons.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:09.160
So it'd be amazing to have that character on
the show, but I think, you know, because they didn't want

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:14.230
too many people coming back from the dead
to spoil the Jon Snow reveal, they just decided

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.410
to cut her out of the show.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:20.089
She also takes control of the Brotherhood
in the Riverlands. It becomes this big storyline.

00:09:20.089 --> 00:09:22.670
The TV show wanted the Brotherhood to head
north.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.290
They wanted Brienne's storyline to take place
with Sansa.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:30.540
So the writers said, behind the scenes, she was
never in any conversations to ever come on

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.540
the show.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:36.000
So it wasn't like they were almost going to do her and then decided not to. They just immediately decided

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.750
that when Catelyn Stark died, that was it, she
wasn't coming back.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:43.410
So, she's a really awesome character in the
books. We can totally talk more about her when

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.580
the next book comes out,

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:49.430
see were her storyline goes. But number two is
Ned Stark. We kind of did get him back,

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:53.360
but not in the way we expected. He's one of
the few characters on the show, and in the

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.880
books, that's in on one of the best well-kept
secrets in the kingdom - who are Jon Snow's

00:09:58.880 --> 00:09:59.880
parents?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.530
What does that mean for the story? Would it
throw the kingdom into chaos?

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:08.120
So, of course the character that knows everything
dies off and now it seems like Bran is the

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.480
path to them learning about that. So they haven't
confirmed whether or not the actor the plays

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.760
Young Ned Stark is going to be coming back
for season seven. He could totally come back,

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.660
it just depends on how they're going to treat
more flashbacks on the TV show, and which characters

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:26.750
they would need for that. Because there are a couple
key characters, including my number one: Rhaegar

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:32.050
Targaryen, the one person that we've heard
a lot about, but have not seen yet. So there've

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:36.540
been numerous storylines that have called him out - Daenerys learned about him through Barristan Selmy,

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.190
we learn a little bit about him
through Robert Baratheon's storyline in the

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:45.730
early seasons of the show, and then now, even
though the show's only implied it, you know behind the

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:50.610
scenes, HBO sort of unofficially confirmed Rhaegar Targaryen is Jon Snow's father.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:55.610
So, it just blows your mind and blows the story
wide open, because you start to see Ned Stark's

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:58.459
motivation for keeping it secret for so long.

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.250
So, he's just a character who is dead now that
we really want back so that we can see some

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.769
of this play out. Because it's some of the best
drama ever, and it's something that fans have

00:11:07.769 --> 00:11:12.740
been waiting for since 1996 when the first
book was published.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:16.950
That's where Ned Stark has the dreams were
he dreams about the Tower of Joy. You get the first

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:22.170
glimpse of what this scene is right here - the
scene that Bran flashes back to. So that's

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:28.270
how long people have waited to get more information
about Lyanna Stark, Rhaegar Targaryen, and Jon Snow.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:32.670
So let me know in the comments, who are the dead
characters that you really want back on the

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.700
TV show?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.779
It doesn't even have to make sense - you know, most of the characters that are alive in the books

00:11:37.779 --> 00:11:42.230
that are dead on the TV show were killed off for
around about reasons. But like George RR Martin

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:43.910
says you know 2016,

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.910
directed by him.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:49.269
I'm sorry, there's a lot of death in "Game
of Thrones". So a lot of that is just to show you

00:11:49.269 --> 00:11:51.959
the casual nature of death in that world.

00:11:51.959 --> 00:11:52.959
Nobody is safe.

00:11:52.959 --> 00:11:54.000
Anybody can be killed off.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:58.200
It doesn't matter how special you think you
are - just remind you of your own mortality.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:02.830
So, if there are any bonus videos that you guys
want me to do, for say like Maester Aemon, the

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:07.740
Targaryens, or anything from Game of Thrones
history, just let me know in the comments.

